<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44293" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔκοσμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>behaving well, orderly,
				decorous</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sol.
				4.33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.42
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ εὔκοσμον αἴρονται φυγήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					481
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ εὔ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκοσμία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.84
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ εὔ</span>., official title at
			Pergamum, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IGRom.</u>
				4.353b3
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>; at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1109.94
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				136
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(ii A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>well-adorned</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖχοι γραφῇσιν εὔκοσμοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>CA</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μως</span>
			<i>in good order</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				628
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότατα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				2.4.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>ornamentally, gracefully</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1120
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαλέγεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Dem.</u>
					11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
